{number: 83}
{title: Amazing Grace}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
A-[G] mazing grace! how [C] sweet the [G] sound,
That saved a wretch like [D7] me!
I [G] once was lost, but [C] now am [G] found,
Was blind, but [D7] now I [G] see.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
'Twas [G] grace that taught my [C] heart to [G] fear,
And grace my fears re-[D7] lieved;
How [G] precious did that [C] grace ap-[G] pear
The hour I [D7] first be-[G] lieved!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Through [G] many dangers, [C] toils and [G] snares,
I have already [D7] come;
'Tis [G] grace hath brought me [C] safe thus [G] far,
And grace will [D7] lead me [G] home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
When [G] we've been there ten [C] thousand [G] years,
Bright shining as the [D7] sun,
We've [G] no less days to [C] sing God's [G] praise
Than when we [D7] first be-[G] gun.
{end_of_verse}
